The base is $(x+5)\text{ cm}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\frac12x(x+5)&=10\\
x^2+5x-20&=0\\
x&=\frac{-5\pm\sqrt{5^2-4(1)(-20)}}{2(1)}\\
x&=\frac{-5\pm\sqrt{105}}{2}
\end{align*}$$
Since the height is positive, reject the negative root.
$$\begin{align*}
x&=\frac{-5+\sqrt{105}}{2}\\
x&\approx2.6\text{ cm}\quad\text{(1 d.p.)}
\end{align*}$$
